1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,240
Good morning, please take a seat. How can I help you?

2
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:10,620
Well, I'm thinking of buying a new car and I'd like some advice.

3
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:15,070
Sure, yes. Had you got any particular make in mind?

4
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:19,860
I'm interested in a Lida. I've had one before and liked it

5
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:21,880
But I haven't really made up my mind.

6
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:29,880
Sure. We've got various models. Umm, right. What about the engine size? Any ideas?

7
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:34,040
The one I've got at the moment's a 1.2 litre engine

8
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:36,734
but I find it a bit slow on long journeys.

9
00:00:36,734 --> 00:00:41,720
I'd like a bit more power this time, a 1.4 should do

10
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:43,900
I don't think I need a 1.6 or anything.

11
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:49,330
Right. Well I think the model you're looking at is the Max. Here's a picture.

12
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:53,260
Oh, yes, have you got one in?

13
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:56,705
Yes. I'll take you to have a look at it in a minute.

14
00:00:56,705 --> 00:01:01,210
I'll just get a few more details. Er... Is there anything else to do with the engine?

15
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:04,920
What kind of gear change do you want? I presume you'd want a manual?

16
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:08,870
I'd want automatic. I've never driven a car with manual gears.

17
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:12,687
Right. Well now, here's the colour chart for the Max.

18
00:01:12,687 --> 00:01:17,650
Have you given that any thought? This blue's very popular at the moment.

19
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:23,000
Yes, it is nice, I like blue. What's it called? 'Royal'?

20
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:23,540
Yes.

21
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:28,850
But actually, I think I prefer this lighter shade here-'Sky'.

22
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:30,450
Yes, that's popular too.

23
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:31,440
I think I'll go for that.

24
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:35,870
You might have to wait a week or so for that colour, but I assume that'd be OK?

25
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:37,500
Oh yes, fine.

26
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:41,440
Well, we can go outside and you can have a good look at one

27
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,376
and perhaps take it out.

28
00:01:43,376 --> 00:01:46,160
But first, can I just ask you about finance?

29
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:50,533
The cash price is going to be somewhere in the region of seven and a half thousand.

30
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:52,076
How would you like to pay?

31
00:01:52,076 --> 00:01:55,420
Are you in a position to pay cash, or would you need credit?

32
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:58,750
I'd like credit provided the terms are reasonable.

33
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:03,710
Well you can discuss that with my colleague in a moment; we have various arrangements.

34
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:08,340
And would you be interested in us taking your present car as part exchange?

35
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:09,050
Yes.

36
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:13,560
OK, fine. So I'll just need some details from you

37
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:16,270
and then we can do a valuation... Is that OK?

38
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:17,850
Fine, yes.

39
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:19,900
Could I have your full name?

40
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:25,660
Wendy Harries, that's H-A-R-R-I-E-S.

41
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:29,110
And is that Mrs... Miss... Ms...?

42
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:30,840
It's Doctor, actually.

43
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:33,890
Oh, right. And your address?

44
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:36,110
20 Green Banks.

45
00:02:36,110 --> 00:02:39,120
Is that 'Green' spelled as in the colour?

46
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,270
Yes, that's right.

47
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:41,290
OK.

48
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,800
Ahon.

49
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:45,510
IS that O-L-T-O-N?

50
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:48,640
Not quite, it begins with an A, not an O.

51
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:51,260
Oh yes, that's in Hampshire isn't it?

52
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:51,870
That's right.

53
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:54,000
And do you know your postcode?

54
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,760
Yes. It's GU8 9EW Do you have a daytime phone number?

55
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:04,651
Well, I work at the hospital but it's a bit difficult to get hold of me.

56
00:03:04,651 --> 00:03:07,500
I can give you a number just for messages

57
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:10,000
and then I'll get back to you when I can. Is that OK?

58
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:10,830
That's fine.

59
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:16,460
It's 0-7-9-8-2-5-7-6-4-3.

60
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:22,130
Fine. And about the car you have now, what make is it?

61
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:23,260
It's a Conti.

62
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:25,920
DO you know the year or the model name?

63
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:31,730
I think it's 1996, and it's called a Lion-like the animal.

64
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:36,600
Then it must be 1994, because they brought out the Fox after that.

65
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,280
Oh right, yes.

66
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,760
Mileage? Roughly?

67
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:44,310
I'm not sure. I know it's less than seventy thousand.

68
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:47,500
OK. What colour is it?

69
00:03:49,650 --> 00:03:54,630
Right, and one last thing. What sort of condition would you say it's in?

70
00:03:54,630 --> 00:04:00,310
I'd probably describe it as reasonable. Do you need to see it? It's parked outside.

71
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:04,050
Not at the moment, no. Perhaps you could call in one day next week...
